      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Use of leuprolide acetate (Lupron) has been associated with angina in men, but there have been no previous reports of angina or myocardial infarction associated with its use in women. The first case of angina and myocardial infarction occurring in a woman undergoing treatment with leuprolide acetate depot is reported."},
